Yabox
=====

Yabox is a small set of native otsos2 userland utilities.

It is not a busybox-style multicall binary.  Every tool is its own ELF
program linked against libc/native and uses the native syscall API directly.

Tools:
- cat - print file data to stdout
- ls - list directory contents
- mkdir - create directory
- rmdir - remove directory
- mv - move file or directory
- touch - create empty file
- rm - remove file
- cp - copy file
- unzip - extract stored zip archives
- profile - run a program under the native trace profiler
- pwd - print current directory
- whoami - print current process permission class

Build:
- make -C ports/yabox

Native API used by directory tools:
- dataDir(API_DATA_DIR_MKDIR, path, NULL)
- dataDir(API_DATA_DIR_RMDIR, path, NULL)
- dataDir(API_DATA_DIR_RENAME, oldpath, newpath)

Native API used by permission-aware tools:
- procPerm(pid)

procPerm(0) checks the current process.  The return value is
API_PROC_PERM_USER or API_PROC_PERM_KUSR.

Native API used by profile:
- traceOpen / traceCtl / traceRead / traceInfo
- procSpawnNative or procSpawn

Examples:
- profile ls /
- profile --full --source syscall,scheduler ls /
- profile --raw --raw-limit 32 --stacks ls /
- profile --csv -o trace.csv --system oven
